# (build 124a) audio.c's record of each track -- what a switch of synth or
# VOICES replays -- holds only the track's own channel. The title theme
# puts track 2 on FM1; the attract's Motavia crawl (its own song) puts it
# on FM2. Up to 124 the record kept the title's FM1 registers under track
# 2, and a switch during the crawl put them back on the crawl's melody on
# FM1: louder, brighter, "less flute like" (The owner), on the chip under
# VOICES EXTRA and on Q either way. Now a track found on another channel
# starts its record again. The route asks during the title and during the
# crawl, then switches the synth there and asks again.
start new
sound render on
wait screen title
wait ticks 600
expect sound-records
wait screen level
wait ticks 600
expect sound-records
synth chip
wait ticks 60
expect sound-records
expect sound playing
